{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2967","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2967","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2967\",\"parent_revision\":\"315a6fbc89f60e63c746dfcb9445efa76ea8f462\",\"root_revision\":\"b83ba4a3e3c035e9b433e84da5df4b4cc6748c7f83661b016dd6016046728129\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-18\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nDiscovered via a hypothesis property test written while reworking #2956's fix (PR #2964). ENTRY_RE (entry_blocks.py) is a regex, re.compile(r\\\"<div><sub>([^<]+)</sub>\\\\s*(.*?)</div>\\\", re.DOTALL), matched via finditer() over a whole section body with no awareness of nesting. If an entry's own content happens to contain a substring shaped like another entry marker (a literal \\\"<div><sub>...</sub>...</div>\\\" text fragment -- e.g. a fact-checker quoting example markup, or documentation about this codebase's own entry-block format), parse_entries() misinterprets it as a second, separate top-level Entry instead of literal content belonging to the first entry.\\n\\nConcrete falsifying example (from the hypothesis property test in tests/test_github_sync.py::TestSectionRoundTripProperty): a Section with ONE Entry whose content is:\\n\\\"<div>\\\\nnested content\\\\n</div>\\\\ n\\\\n<div><sub>2026-01-01T00:00:00Z</sub>\\\\nnested entry-lookalike\\\\n</div>\\\"\\nAfter render_issue_body -> parse_issue_body -> merge_item, the section ends up with 2-3 Entry objects instead of 1 -- content was split apart at the nested \\\"<div><sub>\\\" pattern.\\n\\nScope: this is a different layer than #2956 (which fixed SECTION-boundary \\\"## \\\" detection in extract_sections/parsing.py). This is ENTRY-boundary detection within entry_blocks.py's ENTRY_RE/parse_entries -- a sibling but distinct bug class. Confirmed out of scope for #2956/#2964; the property test's adversarial content strategy was narrowed to avoid this fragment so it stays focused on #2956's actual fix.\\n\\n**Research first**: the fix likely needs the same \\\"structural, not regex-heuristic\\\" treatment #2956 applied at the section level -- either a marko-based or otherwise nesting-aware entry parser, or an escaping/encoding scheme so literal \\\"<div><sub>\\\" text inside entry content can never be confused with a real entry-block open marker. Confirm real-world likelihood/severity (how often does entry content plausibly contain this exact literal string) before committing to a specific fix approach.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>...</sub>\\n\\n...\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Agent task - auto-derived from input, found via hypothesis property test written for #2956\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-18\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"6ade06024a67ccd08072cf50895dd954fb8d93ca51a82b00f39c31497cbf8a87\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPgxT9Q\"}"}